if (!of_get_child_by_name(np, "leds"))
Reason:
The function `of_get_child_by_name()` returns a new reference to the child node, but the original code only uses the return value as a boolean condition and never calls `of_node_put()` on it, causing an OF node reference count leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
np = of_get_child_by_name(phydev->mdio.dev.of_node, "leds");
if (np)
    of_node_put(np);
else
    xway_gphy_init_leds(phydev);
Reason:
The corrected code stores the returned node pointer in `np`, properly releases the reference with `of_node_put()` when the child exists, and only calls `xway_gphy_init_leds()` when the child node is absent. This prevents the reference count leak.

